# "prevent <cut> [of <damage>]. [<also>]": prevent `cut` of the damage `damage` names, or of
# "that damage", the damage in scope, then do `also`, the prevention's additional effect
# [CR#615.1,615.5]. Under `cant`, "<damage> can't be prevented" [CR#615.12].
# TODO(spelling): Taking the prevented damage as a noun phrase and placing `also` as a coordinated
# phrase or following sentence wait on `syl-prevent-damage-phrase` and `syl-spelling-forms-and-runs`.
primitive preventDamage(
  cut: PreventCut,
  damage: Option(WouldClause) = none,
  also: Option(VerbPhrase) = none): VerbPhrase = PreventDamage
